</figure>
<figure id="S6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span><math id="S6.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\CauchyMinValidQBin" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>min</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\CauchyMinValidQBin</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S6.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\calibrationSplit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>ca</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\calibrationSplit</annotation></semantics></math> for the standard multi-class classification experiments. The more challenging <math id="S6.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\datasetFactcheck" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Factcheck</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\datasetFactcheck</annotation></semantics></math> task has a commensurately higher <math id="S6.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\CauchyMinValidQBin" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>min</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\CauchyMinValidQBin</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<div id="S6.T3.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:117.4pt;height:29.1pt;vertical-align:-12.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-17.2pt,4.3pt) scale(0.773894873296448,0.773894873296448) ;">
<table id="S6.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
