<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Verified Generation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For reference, Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ A.2 Verified Generation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> provides the effectiveness over the force-decoded datasets. The support set of the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sdmVerificationLayer" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">verificationLayer</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sdmVerificationLayer</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed from the force-decoded training and calibration data, so this table reflects the held-out classification ability over the verification data, which includes constructed negatives for <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\yVerification=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>verification</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\yVerification=0</annotation></semantics></math>, as described in the main text and illustrated in Table <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.2 Verified Generation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Listing <a href="#LST2" title="Listing 2 ‣ A.2 Verified Generation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> includes the system message and prompts used for the experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Verification results on the <span id="A1.T7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">force-decoded test sets</span> for reference, <math id="A1.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{\prime}=\hbox{\pagecolor{correctPredictionColor}0.95}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2FFF2;" mathbackground="#F2FFF2">0.95</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{\prime}=\hbox{\pagecolor{correctPredictionColor}0.95}</annotation></semantics></math>. See Table <a href="#S6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 6.3 Results: Verified Generation ‣ 6 Results ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> for generation results for the underlying tasks, which reflect real test-time usage. <span id="A1.T7.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2FFF2;">N/A</span> indicates all predictions were rejected, which is preferred over falling under the expected accuracy.
<math id="A1.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=|\text{Admitted}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mtext>Admitted</mtext><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=|\text{Admitted}|</annotation></semantics></math>, the count of non-rejected documents. Additional resolution added to <math id="A1.T7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n}{|\testSplit|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi mathsize="0.980em">te</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{|\testSplit|}</annotation></semantics></math> columns for <math id="A1.T7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\datasetSentimentOODVerification" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SentimentOODVerification</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\datasetSentimentOODVerification</annotation></semantics></math> for reference, but the number of admitted points is effectively 0.</figcaption>
<div id="A1.T7.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:469.8pt;height:131pt;vertical-align:-63.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-91.9pt,25.7pt) scale(0.718668372965007,0.718668372965007) ;">
