<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>JSON structure for the verified generation experiments, with <math id="A1.T8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}^{\rm{ref}}=\modelPhiThreeFiveInstruct" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">phi3.5</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}^{\rm{ref}}=\modelPhiThreeFiveInstruct</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A1.T8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\yVerification=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>verification</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\yVerification=1</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the standard classification tasks, where, e.g., <math id="A1.T8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\yTask=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>task</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\yTask=0</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a negative review for the sentiment task, and <math id="A1.T8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\yTask=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>task</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\yTask=1</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a factually correct statement for the factcheck task. <math id="A1.T8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\yVerification=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>verification</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\yVerification=0</annotation></semantics></math> flips the parity, and is used for constructing negatives for training, and the contrastive basis for rejection at test-time. Recall that the LLM takes as input a system prompt, user prompt, and the document (see Listing <a href="#LST2" title="Listing 2 ‣ A.2 Verified Generation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). At test time, we seek to generate the correct JSON output (i.e., that corresponding to the correct <math id="A1.T8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\yTask" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>task</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\yTask</annotation></semantics></math> label), for instances with <math id="A1.T8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\yVerificationPrediction=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>verification</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\yVerificationPrediction=1</annotation></semantics></math> predicted by the <math id="A1.T8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sdmVerificationLayer" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">verificationLayer</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sdmVerificationLayer</annotation></semantics></math> layer.</figcaption>
